  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Factor the expression $9{n}^{4}-{n}^{2}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice that all of the terms have a common factor of ${n}^{2}.$ To simplify the computation, we can factor out the ${n}^{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n9{n}^{4}-{n}^{2}={n}^{2}(9{n}^{2}-1)\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $9{n}^{2}-1$ using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n{n}^{2}(9{n}^{2}-1)={n}^{2}((3n)^{2}-{1}^{2})={n}^{2}(3n+1)(3n-1)\n$$",
